    "Catholic Home & Family should be built from the much richer domestic/customary research, not these three residual claims."
  ],
  "domains": {
    "FORMATION.FUNERAL_AND_REQUIEM": {
      "claim_count": 15,
      "unsourced_claim_count": 5,
      "claims": [
        {
          "claim_id": "CL07-S05-Q004",
          "stage_id": "CL07-S05",
          "stage_title": "When Death Occurs",
          "layer": "PASTORAL",
          "text": "Christian hope for the deceased does not justify the app declaring the person certainly in Heaven.",
          "source_ids": [],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.FUNERAL_AND_REQUIEM"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL07-S05-Q005",
          "stage_id": "CL07-S05",
          "stage_title": "When Death Occurs",
          "layer": "PASTORAL",
          "text": "The body of the deceased should be treated with Christian reverence.",
          "source_ids": [],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.FUNERAL_AND_REQUIEM"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL07-S06-Q002",
          "stage_id": "CL07-S06",
          "stage_title": "Wake & Funeral",
          "layer": "CURRENT",
          "text": "Current canon law describes ecclesiastical funerals as giving spiritual assistance to the dead, honouring their bodies and bringing the living the consolation of hope.",
          "source_ids": [
            "SRC-CIC83-1176"
          ],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.FUNERAL_AND_REQUIEM"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL07-S06-Q003",
          "stage_id": "CL07-S06",
          "stage_title": "Wake & Funeral",
          "layer": "PASTORAL",
          "text": "Catholic funeral rites can include a Funeral Mass or other lawful funeral forms according to the applicable rite and circumstances.",
          "source_ids": [],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.FUNERAL_AND_REQUIEM"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL07-S06-Q005",
          "stage_id": "CL07-S06",
          "stage_title": "Wake & Funeral",
          "layer": "PASTORAL",
          "text": "The current final commendation and the traditional funeral absolution are not identical rites.",
          "source_ids": [],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.FUNERAL_AND_REQUIEM"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL07-S07-Q001",
          "stage_id": "CL07-S07",
          "stage_title": "Traditional Requiem",
          "layer": "PROFILE_1962",
          "text": "The 1962 Missal contains a distinct Mass-of-the-Dead/Requiem ceremonial profile.",
          "source_ids": [
            "SRC-MR62-REQUIEM"
          ],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.FUNERAL_AND_REQUIEM"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL07-S07-Q002",
          "stage_id": "CL07-S07",
          "stage_title": "Traditional Requiem",
          "layer": "PROFILE_1962",
          "text": "Black is the traditional vestment colour associated with Masses of the Dead in the 1962 framework.",
          "source_ids": [
            "SRC-MR62-REQUIEM"
          ],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.FUNERAL_AND_REQUIEM"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL07-S07-Q003",
          "stage_id": "CL07-S07",
          "stage_title": "Traditional Requiem",
          "layer": "PROFILE_1962",
          "text": "The Dies irae belongs to the traditional Requiem Mass corpus in the relevant 1962 settings.",
          "source_ids": [
            "SRC-MR62-REQUIEM"
          ],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.FUNERAL_AND_REQUIEM"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL07-S07-Q004",
          "stage_id": "CL07-S07",
          "stage_title": "Traditional Requiem",
          "layer": "PASTORAL",
          "text": "The traditional funeral absolution is not sacramental absolution of the deceased person's sins.",
          "source_ids": [
            "SRC-MR62-REQUIEM"
          ],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.FUNERAL_AND_REQUIEM"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL07-S07-Q005",
          "stage_id": "CL07-S07",
          "stage_title": "Traditional Requiem",
          "layer": "PASTORAL",
          "text": "A catafalque is a ceremonial structure or representation and is not the deceased person's body.",
          "source_ids": [],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.FUNERAL_AND_REQUIEM"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL07-S08-Q001",
          "stage_id": "CL07-S08",
          "stage_title": "Burial, Cremation & Ashes",
          "layer": "PROFILE_1962",
          "text": "The 1917 law governing the 1962 context prohibited voluntary cremation.",
          "source_ids": [
            "SRC-CIC17-1203"
          ],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.FUNERAL_AND_REQUIEM"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL07-S08-Q002",
          "stage_id": "CL07-S08",
          "stage_title": "Burial, Cremation & Ashes",
          "layer": "HISTORICAL",
          "text": "The Church's discipline on cremation changed in 1963.",
          "source_ids": [
            "SRC-CDF-AD-RESURGENDUM-2016"
          ],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.FUNERAL_AND_REQUIEM"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL07-S08-Q003",
          "stage_id": "CL07-S08",
          "stage_title": "Burial, Cremation & Ashes",
          "layer": "CURRENT",
          "text": "Current law strongly recommends burial but permits cremation unless it was chosen for reasons contrary to Christian doctrine.",
          "source_ids": [
            "SRC-CIC83-1176"
          ],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.FUNERAL_AND_REQUIEM"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL07-S08-Q004",
          "stage_id": "CL07-S08",
          "stage_title": "Burial, Cremation & Ashes",
          "layer": "CURRENT",
          "text": "Current instruction ordinarily requires ashes to be kept in a sacred place and prohibits scattering them or incorporating them into jewellery or keepsakes.",
          "source_ids": [
            "SRC-CDF-AD-RESURGENDUM-2016"
          ],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.FUNERAL_AND_REQUIEM"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL07-S08-Q005",
          "stage_id": "CL07-S08",
          "stage_title": "Burial, Cremation & Ashes",
          "layer": "CURRENT",
          "text": "The 2023 DDF clarification allows only narrow authority-reviewed possibilities and does not create a general right to divide ashes freely.",
          "source_ids": [
            "SRC-DDF-ASHES-2023"
          ],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.FUNERAL_AND_REQUIEM"
        }
      ]
    },
    "FORMATION.RELIGIOUS_LIFE": {
      "claim_count": 7,
      "unsourced_claim_count": 4,
      "claims": [
        {
          "claim_id": "CL10-S05-Q001",
          "stage_id": "CL10-S05",
          "stage_title": "Religious Life",
          "layer": "CURRENT",
          "text": "Current canon law states that the consecrated state is by its nature neither clerical nor lay.",
          "source_ids": [
            "SRC-CIC83-573-607"
          ],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.RELIGIOUS_LIFE"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL10-S05-Q002",
          "stage_id": "CL10-S05",
          "stage_title": "Religious Life",
          "layer": "CURRENT",
          "text": "Religious profession is distinct from sacramental ordination.",
          "source_ids": [
            "SRC-CIC83-573-607"
          ],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.RELIGIOUS_LIFE"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL10-S05-Q003",
          "stage_id": "CL10-S05",
          "stage_title": "Religious Life",
          "layer": "PASTORAL",
          "text": "Monk and friar are not interchangeable generic labels for every male religious; actual identity depends on the institute and tradition.",
          "source_ids": [],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.RELIGIOUS_LIFE"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL10-S05-Q004",
          "stage_id": "CL10-S05",
          "stage_title": "Religious Life",
          "layer": "PASTORAL",
          "text": "A religious brother is not an unfinished priest or automatically a seminarian.",
          "source_ids": [],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.RELIGIOUS_LIFE"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL10-S05-Q005",
          "stage_id": "CL10-S05",
          "stage_title": "Religious Life",
          "layer": "PASTORAL",
          "text": "Ordinary speech often blurs 'sister' and 'nun', but actual canonical forms of women's consecrated life vary.",
          "source_ids": [],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.RELIGIOUS_LIFE"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL10-S05-Q006",
          "stage_id": "CL10-S05",
          "stage_title": "Religious Life",
          "layer": "PASTORAL",
          "text": "A religious priest is both a religious and a priest; he does not possess a different sacramental priesthood from a diocesan priest.",
          "source_ids": [],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.RELIGIOUS_LIFE"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL10-S05-Q007",
          "stage_id": "CL10-S05",
          "stage_title": "Religious Life",
          "layer": "CURRENT",
          "text": "Not every Catholic community living or working together is canonically a religious institute.",
          "source_ids": [
            "SRC-CIC83-573-607"
          ],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.RELIGIOUS_LIFE"
        }
      ]
    },
    "FORMATION.VOCATIONS": {
      "claim_count": 7,
      "unsourced_claim_count": 6,
      "claims": [
        {
          "claim_id": "CL10-S07-Q001",
          "stage_id": "CL10-S07",
          "stage_title": "Vocations & Milestones",
          "layer": "PASTORAL",
          "text": "Vocation discernment involves prayer, Christian life, counsel and concrete ecclesial processes rather than an app prediction.",
          "source_ids": [],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.VOCATIONS"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL10-S07-Q002",
          "stage_id": "CL10-S07",
          "stage_title": "Vocations & Milestones",
          "layer": "PASTORAL",
          "text": "Entering seminary does not mean a man is already a priest or that ordination is guaranteed.",
          "source_ids": [],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.VOCATIONS"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL10-S07-Q003",
          "stage_id": "CL10-S07",
          "stage_title": "Vocations & Milestones",
          "layer": "PASTORAL",
          "text": "Religious formation commonly distinguishes stages such as postulancy, novitiate and temporary or perpetual profession according to the institute.",
          "source_ids": [],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.VOCATIONS"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL10-S07-Q005",
          "stage_id": "CL10-S07",
          "stage_title": "Vocations & Milestones",
          "layer": "PASTORAL",
          "text": "A newly ordained priest's first blessing is a pious custom; Ad Orientem should not attach an indulgence claim to it without a specific grant.",
          "source_ids": [],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.VOCATIONS"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL10-S07-Q006",
          "stage_id": "CL10-S07",
          "stage_title": "Vocations & Milestones",
          "layer": "CURRENT",
          "text": "The Church's current indulgence grants include a plenary indulgence attached to the priest's first public Mass and to faithful who devoutly assist, under the applicable conditions.",
          "source_ids": [
            "SRC-FIRST-MASS-INDULGENCE"
          ],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.VOCATIONS"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL10-S07-Q007",
          "stage_id": "CL10-S07",
          "stage_title": "Vocations & Milestones",
          "layer": "PASTORAL",
          "text": "Ordination, profession and marriage anniversaries are occasions of thanksgiving, not repetitions of the sacrament or profession.",
          "source_ids": [],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.VOCATIONS"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL10-S07-Q008",
          "stage_id": "CL10-S07",
          "stage_title": "Vocations & Milestones",
          "layer": "PASTORAL",
          "text": "Leaving seminary or religious formation is not automatically a moral failure; formation itself includes discernment.",
          "source_ids": [],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.VOCATIONS"
        }
      ]
    },
    "FORMATION.SPIRITUAL_LIFE.DAILY_RULE": {
      "claim_count": 6,
      "unsourced_claim_count": 4,
      "claims": [
        {
          "claim_id": "CL09-S01-Q002",
          "stage_id": "CL09-S01",
          "stage_title": "The Catholic Day",
          "layer": "CURRENT",
          "text": "The Angelus is a longstanding Catholic devotional practice associated with remembrance of the Incarnation.",
          "source_ids": [
            "SRC-DIRECTORY-POPULAR-PIETY-2002"
          ],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.SPIRITUAL_LIFE.DAILY_RULE"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL09-S01-Q003",
          "stage_id": "CL09-S01",
          "stage_title": "The Catholic Day",
          "layer": "CURRENT",
          "text": "The Regina Cæli has a traditional seasonal relationship to Paschaltide in Marian devotion.",
          "source_ids": [
            "SRC-DIRECTORY-POPULAR-PIETY-2002"
          ],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.SPIRITUAL_LIFE.DAILY_RULE"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL09-S01-Q004",
          "stage_id": "CL09-S01",
          "stage_title": "The Catholic Day",
          "layer": "PASTORAL",
          "text": "Grace before or after meals is a devotional practice rather than a rigid app-enforced schedule.",
          "source_ids": [],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.SPIRITUAL_LIFE.DAILY_RULE"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL09-S01-Q005",
          "stage_id": "CL09-S01",
          "stage_title": "The Catholic Day",
          "layer": "PASTORAL",
          "text": "Short aspirations can be used throughout the day without being treated as mantra-like mechanisms.",
          "source_ids": [],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.SPIRITUAL_LIFE.DAILY_RULE"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL09-S08-Q002",
          "stage_id": "CL09-S08",
          "stage_title": "Build a Catholic Rhythm",
          "layer": "PASTORAL",
          "text": "A small stable prayer rhythm can be better than accumulating an unmanageable number of optional devotions.",
          "source_ids": [],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.SPIRITUAL_LIFE.DAILY_RULE"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL09-S08-Q005",
          "stage_id": "CL09-S08",
          "stage_title": "Build a Catholic Rhythm",
          "layer": "PASTORAL",
          "text": "A devotional routine may legitimately change with work, family, illness, travel, age and vocation.",
          "source_ids": [],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.SPIRITUAL_LIFE.DAILY_RULE"
        }
      ]
    },
    "FORMATION.SPIRITUAL_LIFE.INDULGENCES_AND_REPARATION": {
      "claim_count": 5,
      "unsourced_claim_count": 1,
      "claims": [
        {
          "claim_id": "CL04-S08-Q001",
          "stage_id": "CL04-S08",
          "stage_title": "Indulgences & Reparation",
          "layer": "CURRENT",
          "text": "An indulgence is remission before God of temporal punishment for sins whose guilt has already been forgiven.",
          "source_ids": [
            "SRC-CIC83-992-997",
            "SRC-INDULGENTIARUM-DOCTRINA"
          ],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.SPIRITUAL_LIFE.INDULGENCES_AND_REPARATION"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL04-S08-Q002",
          "stage_id": "CL04-S08",
          "stage_title": "Indulgences & Reparation",
          "layer": "CURRENT",
          "text": "Current discipline distinguishes partial and plenary indulgences.",
          "source_ids": [
            "SRC-CIC83-992-997",
            "SRC-INDULGENTIARUM-DOCTRINA"
          ],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.SPIRITUAL_LIFE.INDULGENCES_AND_REPARATION"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL04-S08-Q003",
          "stage_id": "CL04-S08",
          "stage_title": "Indulgences & Reparation",
          "layer": "CURRENT",
          "text": "A plenary indulgence requires the applicable conditions established by the Church.",
          "source_ids": [
            "SRC-INDULGENTIARUM-DOCTRINA"
          ],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.SPIRITUAL_LIFE.INDULGENCES_AND_REPARATION"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL04-S08-Q004",
          "stage_id": "CL04-S08",
          "stage_title": "Indulgences & Reparation",
          "layer": "HISTORICAL",
          "text": "Older indulgence language using days or years was abolished as the current measure and did not mean a literal number of days removed from Purgatory.",
          "source_ids": [
            "SRC-INDULGENTIARUM-DOCTRINA"
          ],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.SPIRITUAL_LIFE.INDULGENCES_AND_REPARATION"
        },
        {
          "claim_id": "CL04-S08-Q005",
          "stage_id": "CL04-S08",
          "stage_title": "Indulgences & Reparation",
          "layer": "PASTORAL",
          "text": "Reparation and indulgences must not be represented as a spiritual points economy.",
          "source_ids": [],
          "original_destination": "FORMATION.SPIRITUAL_LIFE.INDULGENCES_AND_REPARATION"
        }
      ]
    },
